# Files kept in the repository but NOT shipped in the published archive.
#
# `tool/` holds workspace authoring tools, not consumer tools: they build the
# shared sample document, drive the golden-log comparison, and emit the
# CodeSpecs extracts. Every one of them reads or writes paths in sibling
# workspace projects (`tom_som_conformance`, `tom_specs_model`) that are not
# published, so from a hosted install they resolve onto directories that do not
# exist. Shipping a script that cannot run is worse than not shipping it — it
# reads as a supported entry point.
#
# `example/` is deliberately NOT excluded. Those scripts are the first thing a
# consumer runs, so they must work from a hosted install; they load
# `samples/meridian_order_management.docspecs.yaml`, which ships beside them.
tool/
